      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name was chosen by Lahan, inspired by the famous California seaside town of the same name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/laguna_beach_florida",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1940 the Seahorse Motel opened, marking the first major lodging in the community and signaling post‑World War II growth.",
